    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 1922, the USSR was the first communist state, ruled by the Communist Party from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>.</li><li>It industrialised rapidly under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin">Stalin</a> at enormous human cost, then bore the heaviest losses in defeating Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</li><li>As a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> superpower it rivalled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Gorbachev</a>'s reforms led to its peaceful dissolution in 1991.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The 1924 and later Soviet constitutions formally gave every union republic the right to secede, a provision that only became real in 1990–1991.</p></aside>
    </section>

